# reloadRoute: which tier path the ladder takes after T1/T2, given the guard/process/runner/consent state.
# Characterized from _run_ladder (reload_ladder.py:291-316) and _handle_guard_wedge (reload_ladder.py:212-227).
# Same shape as busysignal: branch precedence broke 3 times historically (guard check must dominate main_dead).
# T1/T2 always run unconditionally; this decision governs the T2.5+ fork.
# First match wins.
DECISION reloadRoute DEFAULT manualRequired
  guardBlockedNoConsent AT 10 WHEN tier.guardWedged AND NOT tier.consentGiven -> guardBlocked
  guardWithConsent AT 11 WHEN tier.guardWedged AND tier.consentGiven -> t5Guard
  mainAliveT3 AT 20 WHEN NOT tier.mainDead -> t3Ahead
  runnerT4 AT 30 WHEN tier.runnerActive -> t4Ahead
  consentT5 AT 40 WHEN tier.consentGiven -> t5Ahead
END
